## 8. Copy and tone

Write like someone who actually works there, not like an agency. Plain, active, specific language tied to the facts in section 2. Australian spelling (tidy, metre, mum). Short paragraphs, no adjective stacking, no exclamation marks, no emoji.

**Bad (generic):** "We provide premier lawn care solutions tailored to your outdoor needs."

**Good (specific):** "We mow, edge and blow down the paths, then check the yard before we leave."

Wherever a claim appears, it must trace back to section 2. Phrases like "fast", "clean" and "neat" are allowed because they mirror real review themes. Avoid superlatives like "best in Brisbane".

